Track 1: Towlines Unbraid the Fog
- Story & Context: It began on the rusted quay of Berth 44 when deckhand Kwame Reid aimed a parabolic microphone into a pea-soup mist so thick it tasted of motor oil and diesel brine. Two lost panamax freighters, blinded by the radar-jamming squall, initiated a frantic three-tone foghorn duel that rattled the fillings in Kwame's teeth, causing his silver concert flute to hum in spontaneous, sympathetic panic. Instead of evacuating the slipway, he cranked a battery-powered sampler loaded with a sluggish Steely & Clevie dembow beat through a bullhorn, toasting over the chaos: "Pull the cord, pull the twine, ship ah tell you stay in line!" just seconds before the gargantuan hulls slid past each other by mere inches.
