Track 2: Who Stitched the Hull Shut?
- Story & Context: Trapped inside the flooded ballast chamber of the decommissioned freighter Oosterdam, audio archivist Anouk Visser nursed second-degree engine burns with salty seawater while the vessel's automated foghorn discharged its lonely low B-flat every ninety seconds into the swirling storm. Abandoned when the skeleton crew evacuated, she braced herself against the sweating iron ribs and played trembling, syncopated flute counter-melodies directly into an underwater hydrophone rigged to a dying cassette deck. Her radio crackled against the vibrating steel bulkhead as she sang into the dark: "You leave me drowned in iron wool, so tell me who stitched the hull shut?" hoping passing cargo convoys outside would mistake her syncopated flute for a harbor signal.
